after referred to as the \"2027/28 K1 Admission Arrangements\") to facilitate a smooth kindergarten admission process and help parents secure kindergarten places for their children in a timely manner.\n\nParents should note that all kindergartens participating in the \"2027/28 K1 Admission Arrangements\" will provide admission information in advance through various channels. Such information may include application forms, guidance notes, school admission guidelines, and information leaflets to facilitate parents in obtaining and submitting applications. Parents should pay close attention to application form distribution and submission dates, application procedures and fees (if applicable), as well as interview arrangements.\n\nThe EDB will assess applicants' eligibility and issue either a Registration Certificate for Kindergarten Admission (RC) or a Kindergarten Admission Pass (AP) to eligible children. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nKindergarten entry age chart and school years by birth month | StarSchools (https://starschools.hk/en/admissions/education-path)\nciteturn2680search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; | S1 allocation strategy EDB SSPA 2027 briefing (PDF) ... A January birth is in the older half of the year (大B, born January to August): two by the first school day, so the PN class falls in 2026/27 and K1 in 2027/28.\n\nChildren born in 2024 are the K1 cohort for 2027/28, the cycle kindergartens are taking applications for now.\n\nThe K1, K2 and K3 columns are the convention, not the regulation. Every kindergarten publishes its own eligible birth dates, and the windows further down show how far apart they sit.\n\n### K1 entry timetable, 2027/28\n\nOpen now\n\n  * 1 Sept - 30 Nov 2026 Open now Registration certificate\n  * Jul-Nov Open now Schools take forms\n  * Oct-Nov Open now Interviews\n  * 11 Dec Offers issued\n  * 7 Jan - 9 Jan 2027 Central registration\n\nSources: EDB Circular Memorandum No. 80/2026 - 2027/28 K1 admission arrangements (PDF)\n\nK1 dates by kindergarten\n\n## Older and younger in one birth year\n\nThe pair of words Hong Kong parents use for the two ends of a birth year, and what changes between them.\n\n### The two words\n\n大B and 細B, the older baby and the younger baby, mark the two ends of a single birth year. Where the line falls depends on the question. For a PN class place it is 1 September, the first school day. For age inside a class it is the spread from January to December, close to a full year.\n\n### A year apart in the PN class\n\nTwo children born in the same year, one in March and one in November, start the PN class in different school years. The March child is two by the first school day and starts at once. The November child waits a year.\n\n### The same class at K1\n\nThe gap closes at K1, which follows the birth year. Both children join the same K1 class, and the one who started the PN class a year earlier arrives having done it. The younger child is not a level behind, only younger in the group.\n\nNot every kindergarten runs a PN class. The kindergartens with care for ages 2 to 3, and how provision below K1 is regulated, are on the two pages below.\n\nKindergartens with age 2-3 careKindergarten guide: provision below K1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n入學申請 (https://clswh.hkfyg.org.hk/2026-2027%E5%AD%B8%E5%B9%B4%E6%94%B6%E7%94%9F%E5%AE%89%E6%8E%92/)\nciteturn2680search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; #### 2027/28學年幼兒班(K1)收生安排 ... (網上報名全年接受申請，本校會面見所有申請入讀的兒童 。) ... EDB’s website on Admission Arrangements for Nursery (K1) Classes in Kindergartens:\n\n# 入學申請\n\n2027-2028年度 幼兒班(K1)及幼苗班(N1)之申請現已開始，如有查詢請致電 2886 8856。\n\n(K1 and N1 applications for 2027/28 are now open. For enquiries, please call 2886 8856.)\n\n#### 2027/28學年幼苗班(N1)收生安排\n\n#### 2027/28學年幼兒班(K1)收生安排\n\n#### 2027/28Admission Arrangements for N1\n\n#### 2027/28 Admission Arrangements for K1\n\n27-28學年入學申請表(Applicatio